.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.TH RCN 1 "September 2026" "rcn 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rcn \- leveled compressor (ratio and compress speed vs each peer class)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rcn
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I COMMAND
...
.PP
.B rcn compress
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I INPUT OUTPUT
.PP
.B rcn decompress
.I INPUT OUTPUT
.PP
.B rcn bench
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I CORPUS
.PP
.B rcn self-test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rcn
is a leveled compressor. Each level is scored on both compressed size
(ratio) and compress throughput against a peer class:
.B \-1
vs
.B lz4 \-9
and
.B zstd \-1
;
.B \-3
vs
.B gzip \-9
;
.B \-9
(default, hybrid) vs
.B zstd \-19
;
.B \-19
vs archival peers.
It stages hash-chain LZ, BWT, LZP, and online logistic mixing, then
entropy-codes with rANS into a .rcn (RCN1) container.
.PP
Invoke
.B rcn \-h
or
.B rcn \-\-help
for a summary; use
.B rcn
.I COMMAND
.B \-h
for per-command help.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B compress
Compress a file into a .rcn (RCN1) container.
.RS
.TP
.I INPUT
Path to the input file.
.TP
.I OUTPUT
Path for the compressed .rcn output.
.TP
.BI \-\-backend \ backend
Entropy backend. Only
.B rans
is built in (default:
.BR rans ).
.TP
.BI \-L \ level\fR, \fB\-\-level \ level
Compression level:
.BR 1
(wire LZ),
.BR 3
(byte CM, no BWT),
.BR 9
(hybrid, default),
.BR 19
(slow bit CM). Negative aliases
.BR \-1 , \-3 , \-9 , \-19
are accepted.
.TP
.BI \-\-mode \ mode
Engine alias:
.B hybrid
(level \-9),
.B slow
(level \-19),
.B fast
(byte CM with BWT trials; not a numbered level),
.B wire
(level \-1), or
.B general
(level \-3).
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose
Print per-block kind, method, and sizes to stderr.
.RE
.TP
.B decompress
Decompress a .rcn (RCN1) container back to a file.
.RS
.TP
.I INPUT
Path to the .rcn container.
.TP
.I OUTPUT
Path for the restored output file.
.RE
.TP
.B bench
Benchmark rcn over every file in a corpus directory (timing and ratio).
.RS
.TP
.I CORPUS
Directory of files to compress.
.TP
.BI \-\-vs \ label
Reserved for SOTA comparison (see
.I scripts/bench_vs_sota.sh
in the source tree). That script prints ratio and compress-speed
win/lose/tie vs peer CLIs when rcn is included (use
.B SKIP_RCN=1
for peer numbers only).
.TP
.BI \-L \ level\fR, \fB\-\-level \ level
Level to bench (default 9).
.TP
.B \-\-fast
Use the byte-level BWT (fast) entropy mode.
.TP
.B \-\-hybrid
Use Hybrid mode (also the bench default when no flags are set).
.TP
.B \-\-wire
Use the level \-1 wire engine.
.TP
.B \-\-general
Use the level \-3 general engine.
.TP
.B \-\-slow
Use Slow bit CM (level \-19).
.RE
.TP
.B self-test
Run the library test suite (via
.BR cargo )
and report PASS/FAIL.
.SH OPTIONS
Global options apply to every command:
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version. Also accepted after a subcommand (for example
.BR "rcn compress \-V" ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (I/O failure, unsupported backend, compress/decompress
error such as CRC mismatch or corrupt container, or failing self-test).
.SH EXAMPLES
Compress a file (level \-9):
.PP
.RS
.nf
rcn compress input.bin output.rcn
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compress at level \-1:
.PP
.RS
.nf
rcn compress \-\-level 1 input.bin output.rcn
.fi
.RE
.PP
Decompress:
.PP
.RS
.nf
rcn decompress output.rcn restored.bin
.fi
.RE
.PP
Bench a corpus directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
rcn bench path/to/corpus
rcn bench \-\-level 3 path/to/corpus
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show help or version:
.PP
.RS
.nf
rcn \-h
rcn \-\-version
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zstd (1),
.BR xz (1),
.BR gzip (1),
.BR lz4 (1)
.PP
Project repository:
.IR https://github.com/rinchen/rcn
